      "id": 1,
      "text": "Gloucester was renamed by Josephus Pigott when the post office opened in 1910, replacing its earlier nickname “Up Straits.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.downeasttour.com/gloucester",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on The Straits, a tidal channel that links Core Sound to the North River, and is bounded by Whitehurst and Sleepy Creeks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gloucester%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1941 the Harkers Island Bridge replaced Gloucester’s private ferry, ending a decades‑long water link that once ferried even circus elephants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        20,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.downeasttour.com/gloucester",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Straits Railway, founded by Lloyd Pigott’s grandfather, is the last traditional boat‑repair shop in Down East, pulling trawlers with a mechanized wench.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.downeasttour.com/gloucester",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Every February Gloucester’s Community Club hosts a colorful Mardi Gras parade, complete with musicians, costumes, and makeshift krewes, celebrating a tradition started in 1992.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.downeasttour.com/gloucester",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Gloucester Community Club Chicken Barbecue, begun in 1955, now raises scholarship money for local high‑school seniors each summer.",
